Bits.Description:
Capture DMA record count. This field defines or reports its timer function and state.

Usage: Configure while capture DMA is idle; request asserts when this number of complete records is available.

Values:
0x0 one record per burst;
0x1 two records per burst;
0x2 three records per burst;
0x3 four records per burst.

Unit: records.

Limits: each record is two 32-bit beats at 32-bit counter width or three beats at 64-bit counter width; the number of APB stream beats per burst must match.

Compare DMA record count. This field defines or reports its timer function and state.

Usage: Configure while compare/update DMA is idle; request asserts when this number of queue slots is free.

Values:
0x0 one record per burst;
0x1 two records per burst;
0x2 three records per burst;
0x3 four records per burst.

Unit: records.

Limits: each record is two 32-bit beats at 32-bit counter width or three beats at 64-bit counter width; the number of APB stream beats per burst must match.

Channel operating mode. This field defines or reports its timer function and state.

Usage: Select while timer_en is zero; a nonzero mode activates exactly one channel function. PWM-input mode is selected through tmr_pwmic_cfg and reserves a fixed channel pair.

Values:
0x0 channel disabled;
0x1 input capture;
0x2 output compare;
0x3 edge-aligned PWM;
0x4 independent one-pulse output.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Capture/trigger edge selection. This field defines or reports its timer function and state.

Usage: Used in input capture and one-pulse trigger mode after synchronization and digital filtering; ignored in compare and PWM output modes.

Values:
0x0 capture rising edges;
0x1 capture falling edges;
0x2 capture both edge polarities;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Input sample divider. This field defines or reports its timer function and state.

Usage: Select the interval between filter samples for this channel; program while its mode is disabled.

Values:
0x0 sample every timer-core clock;
0x1 sample every 2 timer-core clocks;
0x2 sample every 4 timer-core clocks;
0x3 sample every 8 timer-core clocks;
0x4 sample every 16 timer-core clocks;
0x5 sample every 32 timer-core clocks;
0x6 to 0x7 reserved.

Unit: timer-core clock cycles per sample.

Limits: codes six and seven are reserved.

Compare output action. This field defines or reports its timer function and state.

Usage: Used in output-compare mode when the shared counter matches this channel comparison value.

Values:
0x0 set output on a compare match;
0x1 clear output on a compare match;
0x2 toggle output on a compare match;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

One-pulse trigger input selection. Selects one of the eight synchronized and filtered capture inputs as this channel's one-pulse trigger.

Values:
0x0 capture input 0;
0x1 capture input 1;
0x2 capture input 2;
0x3 capture input 3;
0x4 capture input 4;
0x5 capture input 5;
0x6 capture input 6;
0x7 capture input 7.

Unit: none.

Limits: the selected input must be implemented and enabled for capture/trigger use.

